    <div class="intro-box">
      <h3>💡 What is this module?</h3>
      <p>The <strong>utils</strong> module is the largest support package — it handles everything from analyst registry and LLM calling with retry logic, to terminal display, real-time progress tracking, and Ollama/Docker container management.</p>
      <p class="analogy">"Think of it as the <strong>backstage crew of a theater production</strong> — they set up the stage (configuration), manage the lights and sound (display &amp; progress), run the prompter (LLM helpers), and even build the theater itself (Docker/Ollama). The audience (agents) never sees them, but nothing works without them."</p>
    </div>

    <nav class="toc" id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2></nav>

    <h2 id="architecture">Architecture Overview</h2>
    <p>The utils module is a collection of independent utilities, each focused on one concern. The <code>analysts.py</code> file is the single source of truth for all 19 analyst agent configurations. The <code>llm.py</code> file provides the unified <code>call_llm()</code> function used by every agent.</p>
