    <h2 id="deep-dive">Deep Dive</h2>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h4>📋 analysts.py (200 LOC)</h4>
        <p>The <code>ANALYST_CONFIG</code> dict is the single source of truth for all 19 analysts. Each entry has display_name, description, investing_style, agent_func reference, type (fundamental/technical/sentiment), and order.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h4>🤖 llm.py (147 LOC)</h4>
        <p><code>call_llm()</code> is the workhorse — 3 retries, structured JSON output, <code>extract_json_from_response()</code> fallback, and <code>default_factory</code> error recovery. Used by every single agent.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h4>🖥️ display.py (395 LOC)</h4>
        <p>Terminal formatting using colorama and tabulate. Produces colored tables showing analyst signals, portfolio allocation, trade decisions, and performance metrics.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h4>📊 progress.py (116 LOC)</h4>
        <p><code>AgentProgress</code> class with Rich Live display. Tracks agent_status dict, supports update_handlers for WebSocket push, and displays sorted progress bars.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h4>🐳 ollama.py (407 LOC)</h4>
        <p>Full Ollama container lifecycle: start with GPU passthrough, pull models, health checks, stop/restart. The largest file in the module.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h4>🔧 docker.py (123 LOC)</h4>
        <p>Lower-level Docker SDK utilities used by ollama.py for container management, port mapping, and volume mounts.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

